  "description": "Scope: \n-\tThe existing boiler will be replaced with a new unit, with no new penetrations required.\n-\tThree new boilers are proposed in the lift motor room. New penetrations associated with these are indicated on the drawings and will be made through modern blockwork only. No original historic fabric will be lost or harmed, as the floor slab is the only original element in this area which will have the flues pipes coming through it only without affecting any historic features.\n-\tSix new flues will discharge through an existing ventilation grate located above the fire escape double doors. The flue terminals will be colour-matched to the existing grate, ensuring visual continuity.\n-\tThe new system is a condensing boiler system, replacing the current outdated and failing split system. It was selected for its low impact on the listed building, being less invasive, more energy efficient, and lower in carbon emissions. Additionally, it uses readily available parts, unlike the existing system, which is discontinued and difficult to maintain.\n",
